 "sentences": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "text": "He cut the tail off a rat, and let it go.",
   "s": 0.0,
   "e": 1.84
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "text": "You see, the city was crawling with rats, and the officials were terrified of plague.",
   "s": 2.1,
   "e": 5.82
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "text": "So they made a deal. Bring us a rat tail, and we'll pay you one cent.",
   "s": 6.06,
   "e": 9.26
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "text": "The officials are thrilled. Money for vermin? Easiest job in town.",
   "s": 9.58,
   "e": 12.98
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "text": "And it works. Hundreds of tails a day. Then thousands.",
   "s": 13.22,
   "e": 15.72
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "text": "The clerk counting them needs a bigger desk.",
   "s": 16.14,
   "e": 18.12
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "text": "One official stands on the steps and goes, at this rate, there won't be a rat left by summer.",
   "s": 18.36,
   "e": 23.08
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "text": "But summer comes, and the city has more rats than ever.",
   "s": 23.3,
   "e": 26.02
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "text": "Then, people start noticing something weird. Rats running down the street, with no tails.",
   "s": 26.22,
   "e": 30.6
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "text": "Wait, what?",
   "s": 30.98,
   "e": 31.4
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "text": "Well, a dead rat pays you once. But a rat with no tail is still alive.",
   "s": 31.82,
   "e": 35.42
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "text": "It goes back into the sewer, has babies, and every baby grows a brand new one cent tail.",
   "s": 35.62,
   "e": 40.56
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "text": "So nobody was killing rats. They were farming them.",
   "s": 40.8,
   "e": 43.24
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "text": "And when inspectors finally rode out past the edge of the city, they found whole farms, cage after cage, full of rats bred for their tails.",
   "s": 43.42,
   "e": 51.1
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "text": "You see, the officials paid for tails, not dead rats. And people gave them exactly what they paid for.",
   "s": 51.3,
   "e": 57.04
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "text": "The city had hired an entire town of rat farmers.",
   "s": 57.18,
   "e": 59.62
  }
 ]
}